      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Chronic benign pain usually requires treatment with drugs. Three main classes of drugs are used: opiates, non-steroidal anti-inflammatory drugs, and a miscellaneous group which includes psychoactive drugs and a variety of specific agents for individual conditions. The careful selection and combination of drugs, with adequate and appropriate dosage, will bring pain relief in the majority of patients."},
